Z||000001||Raydar||02-15-2000||06:35 PM||||Rebel... Don't feel bad. I'm 42. I bought my first Fiero new (an 85 GT). Traded it three years later for a Firebird. (Two weeks before they announced the cancellation of the Fiero. My dumb a$$.) Saw the error of my ways about two years ago. Bought an 88 coupe. Since then I've also bought a Formula. My wife thinks I'm obsessed.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||02-15-2000||06:40 PM||||I bought an 84 Fiero from a friend of my stepson about 2 years ago. It was a beater but I liked it so well I wanted a "real" one. Bought an 88 Formula almost a year ago. The most "fun" car I've ever owned!!!<P>I am 40. There are quite a few 35+ people on here... we'll have to see how many come forward.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Don't be suprised if you can't stop at one.<P>Welcome to our addiction!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by DRH (edited 02-15-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000003||mwbackus||02-15-2000||06:41 PM||||Well, I am 41.  I have had fast cars since I was old enough to drive.  I think the desire for speed and precise handling is probably more of a genetic thing.  Perhaps they will find the area of gene responsible for this attribute from the human genome mapping project?  Then we can fix all the sports car challenged folks out there and have one hellova good time!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Mike||||reg||6
Z||000004||terryk||02-15-2000||07:19 PM||||46. I wanted something to play with (other than myself) and found my 86 SE about a year ago. Spent a lot of time with Buick SC's and X-11's. Natural progression I guess. Working on a DOHC swap. The V6 auto is a nice cruiser, but can't get out of it's own way otherwise.<P>Turns out the wife drives it more than I do! <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||02-15-2000||07:33 PM||||My name is Dave and I'm a 32 year old, paranoid Fieroholic.  I'll be 35 in just a few short years.<P>mwbackus--This cannot be genetic.  My mother drives an Escort.  Her last car was an Escort and the one before that was a Gremlin.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Robert||02-15-2000||07:34 PM||||You guys are making me feel awfully old.  I bought my first Fiero a year ago, when I was 50.  I’ve always owned a sports car (Datsun 2000, Bug Eyed Sprite, Fiat Spyder 2000), or a performance car (88 Trans-Am GTA).  When my kids were growing up, I had the mini van, but I had a Triumph 750 Bonneville on the side.  I’m enjoying the attention my 87 Fiero GT receives, and look forward to some great trips  with the Golden Gate Fiero Club this Spring.  ||||reg||12
